# UI copy (click-through & Register)

Full law: `docs/build-foundation/10-ui-copy.md`

## Do

- State **facts the persona needs to act** (who, money, state, next event)
- Put structured facts in **UI** (label + value grids/rows). Long prose only in **Terms** / optional Why-price door
- Captions: **one short fact**
- Prefer **periods and commas** in chrome; plain CTAs (`Fund`, `Review terms`)
- Guest landing = **same desk shell as BC** (Campaigns / Meetings / Escrow)
- **Congruence:** same module types rhyme (shell, hairline row, Empty, More, Fact). Don’t force Operator plant or Worker nav into BC’s IA

## Don't

- Narrator ad-lib (“Same person”, “You’re a…”, workshop asides)
- Essay landings that restate escrow math in a paragraph
- Opaque metaphors as primary CTA (“Walk this with Operator”)
- Duplicate stages for the same decision (Invite + Walk twin)
- Icon-square nav + You footer on persona desks when the family uses text nav
- Em-dash slogans / middle-dot metric essays on list rows
- Register jargon in product chrome

## Test

If deleting the sentence does not change the decision → delete it.  
If UI labels + values already say it → don’t also write a paragraph.  
If two personas use the same module type but look unrelated → rhyme toward Guest/BC desk.
